Problem 4.2



                  Q&#039;s 



Do electrochemical potentials equal each other over the salt bridge? (Flow of ions is permitted?)


Each cell is labelled by phase, \alpha\,|\,\beta\,\|\,\beta&#039;\,|\,\alpha&#039;, with

U_{cell} = V^{\alpha&#039;} - V^{\alpha}
Reversible potential @ equilibrium: \mu_e^{\alpha} - \mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} = FU
Species in adjacent phases are at equilibrium.

(a) \mathrm{Cu_{(s)}\,|\,0.001\,M\;CuSO_{4(aq)}\,\|\,0.1\,M\;CuSO_{4(aq)}\,|\,Cu_{(s)}}
\begin{aligned}
\text{LHS: } &amp;\mathrm{Cu \rightleftharpoons Cu^{2+} + 2e^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{Cu}^{\alpha} = \mu_{Cu^{2+}}^{\beta} + 2\mu_e^{\alpha} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha} = \tfrac{1}{2}\big(\mu_{Cu}^{\alpha} - \mu_{Cu^{2+}}^{\beta}\big) \\
\text{RHS: } &amp;\mathrm{Cu \rightleftharpoons Cu^{2+} + 2e^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{Cu}^{\alpha&#039;} = \mu_{Cu^{2+}}^{\beta&#039;} + 2\mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} = \tfrac{1}{2}\big(\mu_{Cu}^{\alpha&#039;} - \mu_{Cu^{2+}}^{\beta&#039;}\big)
\end{aligned}
\therefore\;\boxed{U_{cell} = \frac{1}{2F}\big(\mu_{Cu}^{\alpha} - \mu_{Cu^{2+}}^{\beta} - \mu_{Cu}^{\alpha&#039;} + \mu_{Cu^{2+}}^{\beta&#039;}\big)}
(b) \mathrm{Ag_{(s)}\,|\,AgCl_{(s)}\,|\,HCl_{(aq)}\,|\,H_{2(g)},\,Pt_{(s)}} — with \mu_e^{\alpha} = \mu_e^{\beta}:
\begin{aligned}
\text{LHS: } &amp;\mathrm{AgCl + e^- \rightleftharpoons Ag + Cl^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{AgCl}^{\beta} + \mu_e^{\alpha} = \mu_{Ag}^{\alpha} + \mu_{Cl^-}^{\beta&#039;} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha} = \mu_{Ag}^{\alpha} - \mu_{Cl^-}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{AgCl}^{\beta} \\
\text{RHS: } &amp;\mathrm{H_2 \rightleftharpoons 2H^+ + 2e^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{H_2}^{\alpha&#039;} = 2\mu_{H^+}^{\beta&#039;} + 2\mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} = \tfrac{1}{2}\big(\mu_{H_2}^{\alpha} - 2\mu_{H^+}^{\beta&#039;}\big)
\end{aligned}
\therefore\;\boxed{U_{cell} = \frac{1}{F}\left(\mu_{Ag}^{\alpha} - \mu_{Cl^-}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{AgCl}^{\beta} - \frac{1}{2}\big(\mu_{H_2}^{\alpha} - 2\mu_{H^+}^{\beta&#039;}\big)\right)}
(c) \mathrm{Zn_{(s)}\,|\,ZnO_{(s)}\,|\,KOH_{(aq)}\,|\,O_{2(g)},\,Pt_{(s)}} — with \mu_e^{\alpha} = \mu_e^{\beta}:
\begin{aligned}
\text{LHS: } &amp;\mathrm{Zn + 2OH^- \rightleftharpoons ZnO + H_2O + 2e^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{Zn}^{\alpha} + 2\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta&#039;} = \mu_{ZnO}^{\beta} + \mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;} + 2\mu_e^{\alpha} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha} = \tfrac{1}{2}\big(\mu_{Zn}^{\alpha} + 2\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{ZnO}^{\beta} - \mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;}\big) \\
\text{RHS: } &amp;\mathrm{4OH^- \rightleftharpoons O_2 + 4e^- + 2H_2O} \Rightarrow 4\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta&#039;} = \mu_{O_2}^{\alpha&#039;} + 4\mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} + 2\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} = \tfrac{1}{4}\big(4\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{O_2}^{\alpha&#039;} - 2\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;}\big)
\end{aligned}
\therefore\;U_{cell} = \frac{1}{2F}\left(\mu_{Zn}^{\alpha} + 2\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{ZnO}^{\beta} - \mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;} - \frac{1}{2}\big(4\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{O_2}^{\alpha&#039;} - 2\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;}\big)\right) = \boxed{\frac{1}{2F}\left(\mu_{Zn}^{\alpha} - \mu_{ZnO}^{\beta} + \frac{1}{2}\mu_{O_2}^{\alpha&#039;}\right)}
(d) \mathrm{Pt_{(s)},\,O_{2(g)}\,|\,NaOH_{(aq)}\,\|\,NH_{3(aq)},\,NaNO_{2(aq)}\,|\,Pt_{(s)}} — with \mu_{H_2O}^{\beta} = \mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;} (\mu_{H_2O} = ?):
\begin{aligned}
\text{LHS: } &amp;\mathrm{4OH^- \rightleftharpoons O_2 + 2H_2O + 4e^-} \Rightarrow 4\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta} = \mu_{O_2}^{\alpha} + 2\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta} + 4\mu_e^{\alpha} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha} = \tfrac{1}{4}\big(4\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta} - \mu_{O_2}^{\alpha} - 2\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta}\big) \\
\text{RHS: } &amp;\mathrm{NO_2^- + 6e^- + 5H_2O \rightleftharpoons NH_3 + 7OH^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{NO_2^-}^{\beta&#039;} + 6\mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} + 5\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;} = \mu_{NH_3}^{\beta&#039;} + 7\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta} \\
&amp;\Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} = \tfrac{1}{6}\big(\mu_{NH_3}^{\beta&#039;} + 7\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta} - 5\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{NO_2^-}^{\beta&#039;}\big)
\end{aligned}
\therefore\;\boxed{U_{cell} = \frac{1}{2F}\left(\frac{1}{2}\big(4\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta} - \mu_{O_2}^{\alpha} - 2\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta}\big) - \frac{1}{3}\big(\mu_{NH_3}^{\beta&#039;} + 7\mu_{OH^-}^{\beta} - 5\mu_{H_2O}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{NO_2^-}^{\beta&#039;}\big)\right)}
Problem 4.3
\mathrm{Pt_{(s)}\,|\,FeCl_{2(aq)},\,FeCl_{3(aq)}\,\|\,SnCl_{2(aq)},\,SnCl_{4(aq)}\,|\,Pt_{(s)}} (phases \alpha\,|\,\beta\,\|\,\beta&#039;\,|\,\alpha&#039;)
(a) Reversible potential @ equilibrium: \mu_e^{\alpha} - \mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} = FU; species in adjacent phases are at equilibrium.
\begin{aligned}
\text{LHS: } &amp;\mathrm{Fe^{2+} \rightleftharpoons Fe^{3+} + e^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{Fe^{2+}}^{\beta} = \mu_{Fe^{3+}}^{\beta} + \mu_e^{\alpha} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha} = \mu_{Fe^{2+}}^{\beta} - \mu_{Fe^{3+}}^{\beta} \\
\text{RHS: } &amp;\mathrm{Sn^{2+} \rightleftharpoons Sn^{4+} + 2e^-} \Rightarrow \mu_{Sn^{2+}}^{\beta&#039;} = \mu_{Sn^{4+}}^{\beta&#039;} + 2\mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} \Rightarrow \mu_e^{\alpha&#039;} = \tfrac{1}{2}\big(\mu_{Sn^{2+}}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{Sn^{4+}}^{\beta&#039;}\big)
\end{aligned}
\therefore\;U_{cell} = \frac{1}{F}\left(\mu_{Fe^{2+}}^{\beta} - \mu_{Fe^{3+}}^{\beta} - \frac{1}{2}\big(\mu_{Sn^{2+}}^{\beta&#039;} - \mu_{Sn^{4+}}^{\beta&#039;}\big)\right)
(b)
\mu_{i} = RT\ln(\lambda_{i}) = RT\ln\big(c_{i}f_{i}a_{i}^{\theta}\big)\qquad\text{for } i = \mathrm{Fe^{2+}, Fe^{3+}}\ (\beta)\ \text{and}\ \mathrm{Sn^{2+}, Sn^{4+}}\ (\beta&#039;)
(c)
U_{cell} = \frac{1}{F}\left[RT\ln\left(\frac{a_{Fe^{2+}}^{\theta,\beta}}{a_{Fe^{3+}}^{\theta,\beta}}\left(\frac{a_{Sn^{4+}}^{\theta,\beta&#039;}}{a_{Sn^{2+}}^{\theta,\beta&#039;}}\right)^{1/2}\right) + RT\ln\left(\frac{c_{Fe^{2+}}f_{Fe^{2+}}}{c_{Fe^{3+}}f_{Fe^{3+}}}\cdot\frac{\big(c_{Sn^{4+}}f_{Sn^{4+}}\big)^{1/2}}{\big(c_{Sn^{2+}}f_{Sn^{2+}}\big)^{1/2}}\right)\right]
Assuming f_i = 1:
\boxed{U_{cell} = \underbrace{\frac{RT}{F}\ln\left(\frac{a_{Fe^{2+}}^{\theta,\beta}}{a_{Fe^{3+}}^{\theta,\beta}}\left(\frac{a_{Sn^{4+}}^{\theta,\beta&#039;}}{a_{Sn^{2+}}^{\theta,\beta&#039;}}\right)^{1/2}\right)}_{U_{cell}^{\theta}} + \underbrace{\frac{RT}{F}\ln\left(\frac{c_{Fe^{2+}}\big(c_{Sn^{4+}}\big)^{1/2}}{c_{Fe^{3+}}\big(c_{Sn^{2+}}\big)^{1/2}}\right)}_{\text{Nernst correction}}}
(d) (ferric → 3+, ferrous → 2+)
\big(U_{cell} - U_{cell}^{\theta}\big) = \frac{RT}{F}\ln\left(\frac{1\times10^{-3}}{0.5\times10^{-3}}\left(\frac{0.2\times10^{-3}}{0.7\times10^{-3}}\right)^{1/2}\right)
\;\Rightarrow\;\boxed{U_{cell} = 1.72\ \text{mV vs. standard cell potential}}
Problem 4.7
Ni electrode; V vs. pH diagram.
(a) As shown in class:
Nernst correction for the HER, \mathrm{H^+ + e^- \rightleftharpoons \tfrac{1}{2}H_2}:
\big(U_{H_2/H^+} - U_{H_2/H^+}^{\theta}\big) = \cancelto{0}{\big(U_{H_2/H^+}^{\theta} - U_{H_2/H^+}^{\theta}\big)} - \frac{RT}{F}\ln\left(\frac{p_{H_2}^{1/2}}{c_{H^+}}\right) = -0.0591(\text{pH})\ \text{V vs. SHE}
Nernst correction for the OER, \mathrm{2H_2O \rightleftharpoons O_2 + 4H^+ + 4e^-} (\mathrm{2H_2O - O_2 - 4H^+ = 4e^-}):
\big(U_{O_2/H_2O} - U_{H_2/H^+}^{\theta}\big) = \big(U_{O_2/H_2O}^{\theta} - U_{H_2/H^+}^{\theta}\big) - \frac{RT}{4F}\ln\left(\frac{1}{p_{O_2}\,c_{H^+}^4}\right) = 1.23 + \frac{RT}{F}\ln c_{H^+} = 1.23 - 0.0591(\text{pH})\ \text{V vs. SHE}
(\text{pH} = -\log \mathrm{H^+}; \ln(x) = \log(x)/\log(e); \ln(c_{H^+}) = -2.302\,\text{pH}.)
\mathrm{Ni \rightleftharpoons Ni^{2+}_{(aq)} + 2e^-} — Nernst correction for the Ni electrode:
\big(U_{Ni/Ni^{2+}} - U_{H_2/H^+}\big) = \big(U_{Ni/Ni^{2+}}^{\theta} - U_{H_2/H^+}\big) + \frac{RT}{2F}\ln\left(\frac{\cancelto{1}{c_{Ni}}}{c_{Ni^{2+}}}\right)\;\Rightarrow\;U_{Ni/Ni^{2+}} = -0.257 + \frac{RT}{F}\ln\big(c_{Ni^{2+}}\big)^{1/2}\quad\leftarrow\text{not dependent on pH}
(sketch: V vs. SHE against pH from 0 to 14 — the OER line from 1.23 V, the HER line from 0 V falling to −0.8274 V at pH 14, and the horizontal Ni/Ni²⁺ line at −0.257 V crossing the HER line at pH 4.3; the region below pH 4.3 between them is shaded as “Ni corrosion”.)
Stability:

\big(U_{Ni/Ni^{2+}} - U_{H_2/H^+}\big) &lt; 0 — non-spontaneous @ pH &lt; 4.3 (Ni more negative → will be oxidized)
\big(U_{Ni/Ni} - U_{H_2/H^+}\big) &gt; 0 — spontaneous @ pH &gt; 4.3 (H₂ more negative → will be oxidized)




                  ∴ Ni will be oxidized/corrode below pH 4.3 in acidic solution. 



Problem 4.9
Cu electrode in CuSO₄ electrolyte (\mathrm{Cu \rightleftharpoons Cu^{2+} + 2e^-}); 0.05 M [Cu²⁺].
(a) Calomel electrode (Hg–Hg₂Cl₂ RE): \big(U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}} - U_{Hg/HgCl}\big) = ?
Nernst correction for Cu/Cu²⁺:
U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}} - U_{H_2/H^+} = \big(U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}}^{\theta} - U_{H_2/H^+}\big) - \frac{RT}{2F}\ln c_{Cu^{2+}}^{-1} = 0.337 + \frac{RT}{F}\ln\big(c_{Cu^{2+}}\big)^{1/2}
U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}} = 0.299 V vs. SHE @ 298 K and 0.05 M [Cu²⁺].
Since there is no [Cl⁻] variation:
U_{Hg/Hg_2Cl_2} = \big(U_{Hg/Hg_2Cl_2}^{\theta} - U_{H_2/H^+}^{\theta}\big) - \frac{0.0591}{2}\log c_{Cl^-}^2 = 0.244\ \text{V vs. SHE @ 25 °C and saturated solution [ChemLibreTexts]}
— the RE has its own electrolyte and therefore needs to be corrected depending on the electrolyte used.
\therefore\;\big(U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}} - U_{Hg/Hg_2Cl_2}\big) = 0.131\,[?]\ \text{V}\;\Rightarrow\;\boxed{U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}} = 0.05\ \text{V vs. calomel}}
Transcriber’s note: both values are as written; 0.299 − 0.244 = 0.055 V.
(b) Doing a similar analysis: U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}} = 0.375\,[?] V vs. SHE.
U_{Ag/AgCl} = \big(U_{Ag/AgCl}^{\theta} - U_{H_2/H^+}\big) - 0.0591\log c_{Cl^-}\ \text{[ChemLibreTexts]}\;;\qquad U_{Ag/AgCl} = 0.197\ \text{V vs. SHE @ 25 °C and saturated solution}
\therefore\;\boxed{U_{Cu/Cu^{2+}} = 0.102\ \text{V vs. Ag/AgCl RE}}
(c) Iron electrode: \mathrm{Fe(CN)_{6\,(aq)}^{4-} \rightleftharpoons Fe(CN)_{6\,(aq)}^{3-} + e^-}, with [10x] and [x] respectively.
Nernst correction for the iron electrode:
U_{Fe^{3+}/Fe^{2+}} - U_{H_2/H^+} = \big(U_{Fe^{3+}/Fe^{2+}}^{\theta} - U_{H_2/H^+}\big) - \frac{RT}{F}\ln\left(\frac{c_{Fe(CN)_6^{4-}}}{c_{Fe(CN)_6^{3-}}}\right) = 0.358 - 0.0591\log(10) = 0.298\ \text{V vs. SHE}



                  Results 




U_{Fe^{3+}/Fe^{2+}} = 0.055 V vs. calomel
U_{Fe^{3+}/Fe^{2+}} = 0.101 V vs. Ag/AgCl RE



Problem 5.2
