\therefore\;\frac{d[\mathrm{BX}]}{dt} = -k_3[\mathrm{QA}]_o[\mathrm{BX}]\;(\alpha_j = 1)\;\xrightarrow{\div[\mathrm{BX}]_i,\;\times\varphi/Q_T}\;\frac{d\left(\frac{[\mathrm{BX}]}{[\mathrm{BX}]_i}\right)}{d\left(\frac{t\,k_3Q_T}{\varphi}\right)} = -\frac{[\mathrm{BX}]}{[\mathrm{BX}]_i}\frac{\varphi[\mathrm{QA}]_o}{Q_T}\;\Rightarrow\;\boxed{\frac{dU}{d\tau} = -U\cdot V}
[b] Show \dfrac{dV}{d\tau} = -P_1(V - P_3X) - P_2UV, with P_1 = \dfrac{k_La}{k_3Q_T}, P_2 = \varphi\dfrac{[\mathrm{BX}]_i}{Q_T}, P_3 = \pi_{QA}\dfrac{\varphi}{1 - \varphi} = \dfrac{[\mathrm{QA}]_{o,e}}{[\mathrm{QA}]_{a,e}}.
\underbrace{\frac{d[\mathrm{QA}]_o}{dt}}_{\text{change in conc. of }[\mathrm{QA}]_o} = \underbrace{-k_3[\mathrm{QA}]_o[\mathrm{BX}]}_{\text{reaction in organic layer}} + \underbrace{k_LA([\mathrm{QA}]_{o,e} - [\mathrm{QA}]_o)}_{\text{transport of }[\mathrm{QA}]_o\text{ from aq. layer}}
(\varphi = V_o/V_T, the dispersed-phase fraction; V_T = V_o + V_a; A = interfacial area (effective mass-transfer area); \varphi A = a.) Multiplying by \varphi/(k_3Q_T) and using [\mathrm{QA}]_{a,e} = [\mathrm{QA}]_a:
