\frac{ds_1}{dt} = -\frac{1}{Y_1}r_1v_1\;,\quad v_1 = \frac{r_{G_1}}{\max(r_{G_1}, r_{G_2})}\;;\qquad \frac{ds_2}{dt} = -\frac{1}{Y_2}r_2v_2\;,\quad v_2 = \frac{r_{G_2}}{\max(r_{G_1}, r_{G_2})}
We also know r_1 = 2r_{G_1}, r_2 = 2r_{G_2}:
\therefore\;\boxed{\frac{ds_1}{dt} = -\frac{2r_{G_1}v_1}{Y_1} = -\frac{1}{Y_1}\frac{(2)r_{G_1}^2}{\max(r_{G_1}, r_{G_2})}\;;\qquad \frac{ds_2}{dt} = -\frac{2r_{G_2}v_2}{Y_2} = -\frac{1}{Y_2}\frac{(2)r_{G_2}^2}{\max(r_{G_1}, r_{G_2})}}
Mass balance on B:
\boxed{\frac{dB}{dt} = r_{G_1}v_1 + r_{G_2}v_2}\qquad r_1 = \frac{k_1s_1e_1}{K_1 + s_1} = 2r_{G_1}\;;\quad r_2 = \frac{k_2s_2e_2}{K_2 + s_2} = 2r_{G_2}
(v) The cybernetic variables u_i and v_i were expressed earlier:
u_1 = \frac{r_{G_1}}{r_{G_1} + r_{G_2}}\;,\quad v_1 = \frac{r_{G_1}}{\max(r_{G_1}, r_{G_2})}\;;\qquad u_2 = \frac{r_{G_2}}{r_{G_1} + r_{G_2}}\;,\quad v_2 = \frac{r_{G_2}}{\max(r_{G_1}, r_{G_2})}
— the respective relationships for r_{G_1} and r_{G_2} can be plugged in.
